course: dictionary
lesson: 416
title: Appreciative: thankful and admiring
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Appreciative means thankful. When you are appreciative, you notice that someone has done something kind or good for you, and you show it. Saying thank you is one way to be appreciative.
explain: The word can also mean enjoying and understanding the good things about something. «The audience gave an appreciative cheer.» The audience liked the show and knew what was good about it, so they cheered.
explain: Look at the words around appreciative. In the story, Toad writes a letter «that even the Badger admitted to be modest, grateful, and appreciative». Grateful is very close in meaning to appreciative, so it is a clue. Always ask: what word would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: Appreciative means showing that you are thankful, or enjoying and understanding the good qualities of something.
fact: «An appreciative letter» is a letter that thanks someone.
fact: «An appreciative audience» is one that enjoys a show and understands what is good about it.
fact: Appreciative is an adjective: appreciative, more appreciative, most appreciative.
fact: Grateful is a close synonym, so it can help you work out the meaning of appreciative in a text.
exercise: Mia's gran knitted her a scarf. Mia writes, «Thank you, Gran, I love it and I will wear it every day.» What kind of note is this? | A note asking for money | A note about the weather | A rude note about the scarf | *An appreciative note
exercise: Sam says appreciative means cross. What does appreciative really mean? | Running fast | Very small and quiet | Cross and grumpy | *Thankful, or enjoying the good qualities of something
exercise: The audience clapped, cheered and smiled at the end of the play. Which word from this list describes an audience that enjoys and understands a show? | Bored | Silent | Late | *Appreciative
test: Dad cooked tea after a long day, and Ben said, «Thank you, that was delicious.» Which word describes Ben? | Lazy | *Appreciative | Rude | Forgetful
test: In Toad's letter, «modest, grateful, and appreciative» are listed together. Which word means about the same as appreciative? | *Grateful | Letter | Modest | Toad
exam: What does appreciative mean? | Very tired after a long day | *Thankful, or enjoying the good qualities of something | Loud and noisy | Easy to break
